cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software for academic research, please cite it using the metadata below."
type: software
title: "pi-literature-review"
abstract: "An open and login-free literature review tool, as an extension for
  the Pi coding agent or as a standalone browser app. It provides
  deterministic multi-source search across arXiv, Crossref, OpenAlex, and
  Semantic Scholar plus code repositories, with HTTP-verified identifiers,
  citation graphs, PRISMA documentation, legal open-access PDF downloads,
  and grounded question answering and synthesis over local PDFs with
  page-exact citations. No language model is involved in bibliographic
  search, identifier verification, or the citation path. The system is
  designed to run with local language models and embedding models,
  including on modest hardware, enabling a fully local literature review
  workflow without requiring cloud-based AI services."
